  "categories": {
    "intro": [
      "Something hums beneath the floor, low enough to feel in your teeth.",
      "The walls weep a pale sap that never quite reaches the ground.",
      "Every torch in the room burns without smoke.",
      "The air tastes of old iron and older rain.",
      "Dust here has not moved in longer than any of the local graves.",
      "A single shard of black glass is wedged into the ceiling, point down.",
      "The floor is warmer than it has any right to be.",
      "Something in the corner is breathing, and it is not an animal.",
      "Frost clings to the walls though the season gives no reason for it.",
      "A ring of scorched stone marks the center of the room, old and untended.",
      "The silence here has weight — it presses rather than waits.",
      "Bones are stacked along the far wall, too neat to be accident.",
      "A thin blue light pulses from a crack in the stone, patient as a heartbeat.",
      "The room smells of rot dressed up as flowers.",
      "Every surface is worn smooth in the same direction, as if something dragged through here for centuries.",
      "A faint chime sounds when the wind moves, though there is no wind.",
      "The shadows here fall the wrong way for the hour.",
      "Water drips from somewhere above, striking a rhythm too even to be natural.",
      "The ground is littered with fragments too regular to be rubble.",
      "A carved marker leans in the corner, its writing worn past reading.",
      "Moss grows here in perfect spirals, like something taught it to.",
      "The chill in this room does not lift, no matter how long you stand in it.",
      "Ash covers every surface, fine as flour, undisturbed until you arrived.",
      "A low static crackles at the edge of hearing, gone the moment you turn toward it.",
      "Something has scratched the same mark into the wall a hundred times over."
    ],
    "detail": [
      "You feel it watching before you see where.",
      "Your torch gutters, then steadies, as if something exhaled and thought better of it.",
      "The mark on the wall matches one you have seen before, though you cannot say where.",
      "A chill runs up your arm and does not leave when you step back.",
      "You hear your name, or something close enough to unsettle you.",
      "The floor gives slightly beneath your boot, like it remembers weight.",
      "Something metal clatters deeper in, though nothing moves that you can see.",
      "Your blade hums faintly in its sheath, unbidden.",
      "You catch a smell of copper that was not there a breath ago.",
      "The hum beneath the floor rises to meet your footsteps.",
      "Whatever was breathing has stopped, and the stopping is worse.",
      "Your reflection in the black glass does not quite match your movement.",
      "Dust falls from the ceiling in a slow, deliberate line, as if disturbed from above.",
      "The chime sounds again, closer now, though you have not moved.",
      "You feel the warmth in the stone shift, like something turned over in its sleep.",
      "A second set of footprints joins yours in the ash, going nowhere you can trace.",
      "The blue light dims when you approach, and brightens once you stop.",
      "Your hand finds a groove in the wall shaped like nothing you know, and it fits.",
      "The frost creeps a hand's width further while your back is turned.",
      "Something exhales behind you, and there is no one there.",
      "The static resolves, for half a second, into something almost like words.",
      "The bones shift, just slightly, though nothing touched them.",
      "Your shadow falls a beat behind you, then catches up.",
      "The scorched ring flares faintly hot beneath your boots.",
      "You realize the silence has been waiting for you to notice it."
    ]
  }
}
